{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1411129-solar-war-remake-i-am-once-again-asking-you-all-to-read-d","id":1411129,"title":"[Solar War Remake] I am, once again, asking you all to read :D","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-30T15:59:46-07:00","id":1411129,"title":"[Solar War Remake] I am, once again, asking you all to read :D","content":"Another fortnight, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oIBGt9gagKCk2Pipun6-p_83kJADCiGHEAEZvENRR84/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">another charm set</a>!<br /> <br /> The Solar War charmset's weirdness stems not so much from a wild incoherence as integrity or convoluted construction like craft, but more from a blandness.<br /> <br /> The trend of going for more coherent effects remains, and this time around I put added more pomp, more circumstance, shifted things around a little and, finally, added a handful of personal-scale combat enhancers that play into &quot;dominating the battlefield&quot;.<br /> <br /> Expect to see even nastier Tiger Warriors, crazy schemes, sacred fortifications and even warriors denying their own deaths because they are too busy winning. Dining in Hell can wait a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As usual, everyone is welcome to it, and is welcome to chip in with whatever ideas you want. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T02:12:17-07:00","id":1411181,"title":"","content":"Added few comments and added to my Home-brew folder <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think some Charms are a bit &quot;mechanically annoying&quot; even if effective, like the one that make enemies not reset the specific onslaught inflicted by a gambit for Essence turns; it makes things hard to track. <br /> <br /> I really like your new Warrior Training technique, and the Lieutenant Charm that follows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T01:46:03-07:00","id":1417524,"title":"","content":"I really like, &quot;Canny Misdirection&quot; through &quot;Clever Diversion Arrangements&quot;, I personally have always found gambits to be a cool idea and using them more often could be great. Its one of the reasons, I have added a number of other weapons to the base game that I think should have adjusted keywords such as the Tiger Fork (Short Spear with a tip shaped and used like a Sai, gets disarming but loses Thrown).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T06:56:37-07:00","id":1417542,"title":"","content":"Aye. My preferred way to do it is to buff gambit weapon tags from &quot;-1 diff&quot; to &quot;perform gambit reflexively&quot;. That particular type of houseruling goes against my goal with these remakes, but it's a nice direction to take. <br /> <br /> (other buffs to weapon tags include Piercing ignoring Ov+Str soak of any type and ignoring Ov hardness, chopping add +3 to any raw damage rather than just withering)<br /> <br /> <br /> If you adopt houserules that let you reflexively gambit such as this one, Canny Misdirection may cost 2m instead of 3m, and its effect changes to &quot;give a gambit tag to the attack, and if the weapon already has it lower gambit diff by 1&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}